##### "IDENTIFICATION": Jump to "\_parse\_identification\_statement", Check the config header
> borderColor=`#0000FF`,fillColor=`#121212`,textColor=`#FFFFFF`

- NOTE
<pre>Every BOT file need the configuration header to notice the parser that this config file's id, follow rules of the parser's version, data's encode, and readonly or not (like global lock).

When in here, this configuration file's header like this:
[Identify word signal] + [What type you want to identify] + [identify value]

Example:
IDENTIFICATION CONFIGURATION-ID &quot;XXX&quot;;  # Identify this config file's global id is &quot;XXX&quot;.

IDENTIFICATION CONFIGURATION-VERSION 1.0;  # Identify this config file is follow the rules of parser which version is 1.0, so you won't need to change the config file when you want to update the parser.

IDENTIFICATION CONFIGURATION-ENCODE &quot;UTF-8&quot;;  # Tell that what need to decode with. This parser will change the rule and reload the file with correct encode.

IDENTIFICATION CONFIGURATION-READONLY TRUE;  # Global lock, you can use this to reject all the change-requests from the developer.</pre>

